  "notes": "University Park, no formal tracks. The BBH department catalog was already largely populated. Multi-campus note (2026-08-27): this is a Pattern A shared-curriculum major, not a Behrend-specific program -- Behrend's own bulletin page (bulletins.psu.edu/undergraduate/colleges/behrend/biobehavioral-health-bs/) prescribes the exact same core courses as this plan (BBH 101, BBH/AFAM 302, BBH 310, BBH 311, BBH 316, BBH 411W, BBH/HPA 440, BIOL 110, BIOL 161, BIOL 163, NUTR 251, PSYCH 100) and the exact same elective-category structure and department lists (Genetics/Evolution: BBH 210/BIOL 133/BIOL 222; Ethics: BBH 301W/PHIL 110/PHIL 132; Basic Science Electives: the same ANTH/BIOL/BMB/CHEM/EARTH/EGEE/FDSC/GEOG/MICRB/PHYS/PSYCH/VBSC list; Human Development/Health Electives: the same CSD/HDFS/HPA/KINES/NURS/NUTR/PSYCH list; Statistics: STAT 200/STAT 250; Advanced BBH Electives: the same footnoted course list), just taught on a different suggested per-term schedule -- consistent with Behrend's own page noting up to 24 credits of the major may be required at University Park, Greater Allegheny, New Kensington, or World Campus, i.e. this is one university-wide major delivered at multiple campuses rather than a separate Behrend department/curriculum. Added \"Erie\" to this plan's campus array rather than building a new BBH-suffixed file, per this session's Pattern A rule. Explicitly scheduled ENGL 15 (Semester 1) rather than a generic GWS slot for the entrance writing requirement, matching this session's established convention. Post-prereq-parser-fix repair: STAT 200/STAT 250's real prereq is MATH 21, which was never in this plan at all (MATH wasn't even in the departments list) -- and MATH 21 itself real-chains through MATH 4 and MATH 3, leaving STAT 200 and everything after it (BBH 310, BBH 440, BBH 411W) permanently unschedulable. Added MATH to departments and MATH 3 (Semester 1), MATH 4 (Semester 2), MATH 21 (Semester 3) explicitly to complete the real chain. Handbook verification pass: the BBH undergraduate handbook at hhd.psu.edu/bbh/biobehavioral-health-undergraduate-handbook is access-restricted (403, PSU-authenticated users only) so it could not be read -- but the live bulletin's own Suggested Academic Plan (bulletins.psu.edu, 2026-27 edition) publishes exact, numbered footnote course lists for every one of this major's elective categories, which the plan previously modeled as fully generic unfillable placeholders. Wired all five to their real footnoted lists as explicit 'options' pools (same convention as this plan's other multi-option course items), verified credit-count/slot-count against the same suggested plan (all matched exactly -- no credit-count discrepancy despite first appearances): 'Health and Developmental Science Elective' (footnote 2, CSD/HPA/HDFS/KINES/NURS/NUTR/PSYCH/RPTM/RHS/SPAN courses), 'Life Sciences Elective' (footnote 3, CHEM/MICRB/BIOL), 'Basic Science Elective' (footnote 1, a much wider ANTH/BMB/BIOL/CHEM/EARTH/EGEE/EMSC/FDSC/GEOG/KINES/MICRB/PHYS/PSYCH/VBSC list), 'Health Promotion Elective' (footnote 6), and 'BBH Additional Elective' (footnote 5, full list for the two '2XX-4XX' slots, 400-level-only subset for the two '4XX' slots -- the real requirement is a single pooled 'select 12, at least 6 at the 400 level', which this 2-generic+2-400-level split already satisfies). Omitted the footnote 2 list's three CMAS codes (CMAS 258/465/466) -- no CMAS catalog exists in this app and that code prefix is a Commonwealth-campus Communication Arts and Sciences designation, not clearly offered at this plan's University Park/World Campus end campus; excluded rather than guessed. Excluded BBH 302 from the 'BBH Additional Elective' options (footnote 5 lists it, but it's a separate required Prescribed Course in this same plan already, at Semester 5) to avoid a confusing duplicate listing, even though the engine's own completed-code exclusion would have made it harmless either way. Corrected 'FDSC 406' (footnote 1's own text) to the real current code 'FDSC 406W', confirmed against this app's own scraped fdsc_catalog.json. A handful of footnote-listed codes (BIOL 246W, BIOL 475N, VBSC 231, EMSC 101, FDSC 406W-adjacent GEOG 110, RPTM 100, KINES 141/180/233, HDFS 258, NUTR 111/456/466, BBH 417) aren't present in this app's own scraped catalogs for their departments (a scraping gap, not a bulletin error) -- left them in the options lists since they're real bulletin-listed codes, but they'll behave as unchecked fallback options (no prereq gate, generic display name) until those catalogs are refreshed.",
